    "video_with_text_RCdeDb": {
      "type": "video-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_WkfWbW": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Restore Your Neck's Natural Curve to Ease <strong>Neck Pain&nbsp;</strong>",
            "heading_size": "title-sm",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle",
            "highlighted_reveal": false
          }
        },
        "text_kAqtPj": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Modern activities push the head further forward than what's normal. This causes the muscles to tighten and compensate, leaving the neck <strong>stuck in this position</strong> all the time.</p><p>What <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">makes things worse</span> is that when muscles are stressed and contracted, they <strong>choke off their own blood supply.</strong> So even though your body is desperately trying to pump more blood into the neck area to strengthen the muscles, it simply can't.</p><p>To help restore the neck's natural curve, we equipped the Questprops &nbsp;with <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">electrical muscle stimulation, or EMS</span>. This technology <strong>contracts the muscles through gentle electrical currents</strong> — basically mimicking exercise.</p><p>When you lay down on it, the Cradle holds your neck at the <strong>26° angle</strong>, which is the position <strong>designed to support decompression of the cervical spine.</strong> At the same time, the small electrical impulses encourage your muscles to <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">contract and act like pumps, naturally pushing blood through the neck</span> and improving circulation.</p><p>This helps muscles <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">relax and return to their natural position</span>, easing pressure on the cervical spine, and <strong>addressing the source of the neck pain.</strong></p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
